Scale the libp2p regtest PoC to configurable topologies of up to three miners,
ten signer/companion-node pairs, and five outsider followers. Add per-actor
authenticated telemetry, bounded host-driven chaos testing, restart-safe
Bitcoin mining, retryable Epoch 4 fixture deployment, and full-topology
canonical-convergence verification.

Require chaos recovery to start stopped services as well as unpause paused
services, then prove each recovered target is running and healthy before the
next disruption.

Allow the collector-outage chaos gate to require an authenticated
`telemetry-blind-spot` incident before recovery, proving that chain progress is
independent of telemetry and that the observer labels stale coverage honestly.

Publish each signer's reconstructed state-machine update when its native
network handle is installed, preventing a simultaneous signer-set restart from
waiting circularly for a state transition before protocol-version agreement.
